### (2/5) Warn on unsupported Badge icon suffixes

**Severity:** `low`

A typo in the documented Badge icon style currently falls through to the regular glyph without an `InvalidValue` warning. This preserves the regular fallback while reporting unsupported suffixes; apply this body change with all four remaining suggestions in the atomic group.

```suggestion
        if (comma < 0)
        {
            return (reference.Trim(), false);
        }

        var name = reference[..comma].Trim();
        var style = reference[(comma + 1)..].Trim();
        if (style.Equals("filled", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        {
            return (name, true);
        }

        if (!style.Equals("regular", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
        {
            warnings.Add($"icon '{name}' has unknown style '{style}'; using regular.");
        }

        return (name, false);
```

### (4/5) Keep valid-form tests warning-free

**Severity:** `low`

Update the existing valid-reference test to pass a warning collection after the parser signature change, and confirm valid references remain warning-free. Apply this with all four remaining suggestions in the atomic group.

```suggestion
        var warnings = new List<string>();
        Assert.AreEqual(("Checkmark", true), FluentIconGlyphs.ParseReference("Checkmark,filled", warnings));
        Assert.AreEqual(("Checkmark", false), FluentIconGlyphs.ParseReference("Checkmark, Regular", warnings));
        Assert.AreEqual(("Checkmark", false), FluentIconGlyphs.ParseReference(" Checkmark ", warnings));
        Assert.AreEqual(0, warnings.Count);
```

### (5/5) Cover invalid Badge style suffixes

**Severity:** `low`

Exercise the Badge model with a valid icon and a misspelled style so the fallback glyph is retained and a warning is observable. Apply this with all four remaining suggestions in the atomic group.

```suggestion
    [TestMethod]
    public void BadgeIconReferencesWarnForUnknownStyles()
    {
        var warnings = new List<string>();
        var model = BadgeModel.Parse("""{ "icon": "Calendar,fillled" }""", warnings);

        Assert.AreEqual("\uE787", model.IconGlyph);
        Assert.AreEqual(1, warnings.Count);
        Assert.AreEqual("icon 'Calendar' has unknown style 'fillled'; using regular.", warnings[0]);
    }
}
```

